A.lJR=new B.a(" In a neonatal subgroup analysis (n=4426) of a large observational study (n=22,258), aminocaproic acid had greater bleeding requiring surgical intervention compared with aprotinin ",!1,!1,!1)
A.ndV=new B.a(". There was higher blood loss with aminocaproic acid (46 mL/kg) compared with aprotinin (36 mL/kg), but no differences in need for transfusion or requirement for surgical revision in 235 neonates who underwent CPB in a nonrandomized study ",!1,!1,!1)
A.m9S=new B.a(". There was no difference in blood loss, requirement for surgical revision due to bleeding, or need for transfusion between tranexamic acid and aminocaproic acid in 105 neonates who underwent CPB in a nonrandomized study ",!1,!1,!1)
