A.QN=new B.a(" There was no difference in clinical response between echinocandins and amphotericin B (OR 1.38; 95% CI, 0.68 to 2.8) for the treatment of suspected or confirmed invasive candidiasis in a meta-analysis (n=5; 354 neonates and children). Antifungals included were micafungin, caspofungin, amphotericin B deoxycholate, and liposomal amphotericin B. Subanalysis demonstrated no difference in other comparisons including mycological response, mortality, recurrence of candida infection, type of echinocandin, different risk groups (high-risk, low-risk, or neutropenic groups), and type of use (targeted or empirical). Discontinuation due to adverse effects were higher with amphotericin B than the echinocandins (OR 0.3; 95% CI, 0.12 to 0.76) ",!1,!1,!1)
