A.lH2=new B.a(" BPD was significantly reduced by 25% with high-dose caffeine therapy compared with standard-dose therapy when used for any indication (RR, 0.75; 95% CI, 0.6 to 0.94; 5 studies, 723 patients). When broken down by indication, the results were only significantly in favor of high-dose caffeine in those treated for prevention of reintubation; findings were not significant for treatment or prevention of apnea ",!1,!1,!1)
