A.lFm=new B.a("A significant reduction in extubation failure (22% vs 47%), the frequency of apnea (9 vs 16), and days of documented apnea (2.5 days vs 5 days) were observed with high-dose oral caffeine citrate compared with standard dose (20 mg/kg/day loading dose, 10 mg/kg/day maintenance) in a randomized, double-blind study in 120 preterm (less than 32 weeks gestation; 10 days or younger) with apnea of prematurity. Tachycardia was significantly more frequent (23% vs 8%) in the high-dose vs low-dose group ",!1,!1,!1)
