A.mX9=new B.a("Fewer infusion-related reactions and tissue damage (eg, purple glove syndrome) compared with phenytoin. Hypotension and cardiac arrhythmias have been reported. Dose related adverse events include nystagmus (total level, 15 to 25 mg/L) and ataxia and mental status changes (total level greater than 30 mg/L). Movement disorders (bradykinesia and choreoathetosis) may also occur rarely. Minor venous irritation upon IV administration. Vomiting is common in children. Long-term effects of therapy include gingival hyperplasia, coarsening of the facies, hirsutism, hyperglycemia, and hypoinsulinemia. Fosphenytoin drug interactions are similar to phenytoin (ie, carbamazepine, cimetidine, corticosteroids, digoxin, furosemide, phenobarbital, and valproate) ",!1,!1,!1)
