A.mxh=new B.a("Pyridoxine is a coenzyme in amino acid and carbohydrate metabolism required for the conversion of tryptophan to both niacin and neurotransmitter serotonin and conversion of dopa to dopamine. It is also required for the synthesis of the inhibitory neurotransmitter gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA). Pyridoxine-dependent seizures are a result of defective binding of pyridoxine in the formation of GABA. They typically present in the neonatal period or early infancy; however, seizures can occur for the first time at up to 3 years of age. In addition to seizures, presentation may include hypothermia, jitteriness, encephalopathy, abdominal distension, and vomiting. Administration of pharmacologic doses of pyridoxine will correct this GABA deficiency ",!1,!1,!1)
