A.bL1=new B.d("Cystic fibrosis maintenance (Bronchitol; after passing tolerance test):",!0)
A.bpF=new B.d("Child \u22656 yr and adult (limited data <18 yr): Inhale the contents of 10 capsules (400 mg) BID (every morning and 2\u20133 hr before bedtime). Use an inhaled short-acting bronchodilator 5\u201315 min prior to each dose.",!1)
A.duh=s([A.bL1,A.bpF],t.I)
A.bNc=new B.l("Inhalational use (see remarks):",A.duh,null)
A.fya=s([A.c0D,A.bNc],t.T)
A.hbH=s(["Contraindicated in severe renal disease, active intracranial bleed, dehydration (especially severe hypovolemia), prior hypersensitivity to mannitol, and pulmonary edema. May cause circulatory overload and electrolyte disturbances. For hyperosmolar therapy, keep serum osmolality at 310\u2013320 mOsm/kg. Do not use with aminoglycosides as this may enhance nephrotoxicity risk.","Larger doses may require fluid bolus to prevent hypotension. May cause hypovolemia, headache, acute kidney injury, and polydipsia. Reduction in ICP occurs in 15 min and lasts 3\u20136 hr.","Caution: Drug may crystallize at low temperatures with concentrations \u226515%; redissolve crystals by warming solution up to 70\xb0C with agitation. Use an in-line filter (\u22645 micron).","INHALED USE (Bronchitol): Do not puncture the capsule more than once and do not swallow capsule. Use an inhaled bronchodilator prior to each dose. Patients are instructed to exhale fully first, then place inhaler device in the mouth by closing the lips around the mouthpiece, and take a steady, deep breath, inhaling the contents of the capsule, followed by holding the breath for 5 sec before exhaling. Repeat the process again if powder is still left. Each inhaler device should be replaced after 7 days of use. Use of this product is contraindicated if the patient fails the Bronchitol Tolerance Test (BTT); see product information for testing procedure and passing criteria. Common side effects from the BTT include nausea, retching, chest discomfort, dizziness, headache, cough, dyspnea, respiratory tract pain, nasal discharge, throat irritation, and wheezing. Common side effects during maintenance therapy include arthralgia, cough, throat pain, pulmonary bacterial infection (positive sputum), and fever. Aridol product is indicated for the assessment of bronchial hyperresponsiveness in children \u22656 yr and adults."],t.s)
A.chl=new B.Z("MANNITOL","Osmitrol, and generics, inhalation: Bronchitol and Aridol","Osmotic diuretic",A.dxT,A.fya,A.hbH,"","Harriet Lane Handbook, 24th ed. \u2014 pp. 1091\u20131092")
A.hZD=s(["Chewable tabs: 100 mg (may be swallowed whole or chewed); contains saccharin"],t.s)
A.aSt=new B.d("Pinworms (Enterobius): 100 mg PO \xd7 1, repeat in 2 wk if not cured.",!1)
A.aTV=new B.d("Hookworms, roundworms (Ascaris), and whipworm (Trichuris): 100 mg PO BID \xd7 3 days. Repeat in 3\u20134 wk if not cured. Alternatively, may administer 500 mg PO \xd7 1 and repeat in 3\u20134 wk if not cured.",!1)
