A.eFp=s(["Not recommended for children <8 yr and during the last half of pregnancy due to risk of permanent tooth discoloration. Use with caution in renal failure; lower dosage may be necessary. High incidence of vestibular dysfunction (30%\u201390%). Nausea, vomiting, allergy, increased intracranial pressure (e.g., pseudotumor cerebri), photophobia, and injury to developing teeth may occur. Hepatitis, including autoimmune hepatitis, liver failure, hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., anaphylaxis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, erythema multiforme), and serum sickness\u2013like and lupus-like syndrome have been reported.","May increase effects/toxicity of warfarin and decrease the efficacy of live attenuated oral typhoid vaccine. May be administered with food but NOT with milk or dairy products. See Tetracycline for additional drug/food interactions and comments.","TOPICAL USE: Dosage form is flammable; avoid smoking during and immediately after application. Not for oral, ophthalmic, or intravaginal use. Headache is the most common side effect. Hyperpigmentation, erythema, dryness, and itching have also been reported."],t.s)
