A.h8L=s(["R-isomer of racemic albuterol. Side effects include tachycardia, palpitations, tremor, insomnia, nervousness, nausea, and headache.","Clinical data in children demonstrate levalbuterol is as effective as albuterol with fewer cardiac side effects at equipotent doses (0.31\u20130.63 mg levalbuterol ~2.5 mg albuterol). However, when higher doses of levalbuterol (1.25 mg) were compared to 2.5 mg albuterol, changes in heart rate were similar.","More frequent dosing may be necessary in asthma exacerbation."],t.s)
