A.fa1=s(["PO administration may cause gastrointestinal disturbance and ulceration. Oral liquid supplements should be diluted in water or fruit juice prior to administration. Sustained-release tablets must be swallowed whole and NOT dissolved in the mouth or chewed.","Do not administer IV potassium undiluted. IV administration may cause irritation, pain, and phlebitis at the infusion site. Rapid or central IV infusion may cause cardiac arrhythmias. Patients receiving infusion >0.5 mEq/kg/hr (>20 mEq/hr for adults) should be placed on an electrocardiographic monitor."],t.s)
