A.etw=s(["May cause nausea, vomiting, abdominal cramps, diarrhea, and body odor. Seizures have been reported in patients with or without a history of seizures.","Safety in end-stage renal disease (ESRD) has not been established. High doses to severely compromised renal function or ESRD on dialysis may result in accumulation of potentially toxic metabolites (trimethylamine and trimethylamine-N-oxide). Serious hypersensitivity reactions, including anaphylaxis, have been reported with IV use mostly in ESRD patients undergoing dialysis.","Give bolus IV infusion over 2\u20133 min."],t.s)
