A.eP7=s(["Contraindicated in treating perioperative pain for coronary artery bypass graft surgery. May cause GI bleeding, thrombocytopenia, heartburn, headache, drowsiness, vertigo, and tinnitus. Use with caution in patients with GI disease, cardiac disease (risk for thrombotic events, myocardial infarction [MI], stroke), or renal or hepatic impairment, and those receiving anticoagulants. Drug reactions with eosinophilia and systemic symptoms (DRESS), and serious skin reactions (e.g., SJS, TEN, fixed drug eruption, and generalized bullous fixed drug eruption) have been reported. False-positive test for urine cannabinoid screen may occur.","Use is NOT recommended for moderate/severe renal impairment (CrCl <30 mL/min). See Ibuprofen for other side effects.","Administer doses with food or milk to reduce GI discomfort."],t.s)
