A.hfx=s(["Monitor renal, hepatic, electrolyte, and hematologic status closely. Thrombocytopenia, anemia, leukopenia, hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, diarrhea, respiratory failure, skin rash, nephrotoxicity, and increases in liver enzymes and bilirubin may occur. See Conventional Amphotericin B for drug interactions.","Highest concentrations achieved in spleen, lung, and liver based on human autopsy data from one heart transplant patient. CNS/CSF levels are lower than amphotericin B, liposomal (AmBisome). In animal models, concentrations are higher in the liver, spleen, and lungs but the same in the kidneys when compared with conventional amphotericin B. Pharmacokinetics in renal and hepatic impairment have not been studied.",u.n],t.s)
