A.fjp=s(["Closely monitor renal, hepatic, electrolyte, and hematologic status. Thrombocytopenia, anemia, leukopenia, tachycardia, hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, hypocalcemia, hyperglycemia, diarrhea, dyspnea, skin rash, low back pain, nephrotoxicity, and increases in liver enzymes and bilirubin may occur. Rhabdomyolysis has been reported. Safety and effectiveness in neonates have not been established as lipid-based formulations may have reduced tissue penetration as compared with conventional formulations in neonates. See Conventional Amphotericin B for drug interactions.","Compared with conventional amphotericin B, higher concentrations are found in the liver and spleen, and similar concentrations are found in the lungs and kidneys. CNS/CSF concentrations are higher than other amphotericin B products. Pharmacokinetics in renal and hepatic impairment have not been studied.",u.n,"False elevations of serum phosphate have been reported with the PHOSm assay (used in Beckman Coulter analyzers)."],t.s)
