A.fPR=s(["Contraindicated in pregnancy. Pregnancy testing 2 wk prior to use and initiation of use during a normal menstrual period have been recommended. Avoid use in abraded or eczematous skin or with other medications or cosmetics with drying effects, or medications that can cause photosensitivity.","Tazarotene is a retinoid prodrug that is converted to its active form, the cognate carboxylic acid of tazarotene (AGN 190299), by rapid deesterification in animals and humans.","Common side effects include erythema, dry skin, skin irritation/pain (including blistering and skin desquamation), pruritus, and worsening of psoriasis.","Avoid contact with mucous membranes. The foam dosage form is flammable; avoid fire, flame, or smoking during or immediately after use."],t.s)
